    "Fetch Album Artwork" : {

    },
    "ShoutKit App — GPL-3.0" : {

    },
    "ShoutKit is free software — everything works whether or not you donate. On beta builds you can also send feedback by taking a screenshot in TestFlight." : {

    },
    "ShoutKit's code name is Holmdel, for the Bell Labs site in Holmdel, New Jersey, where in 1964 Arno Penzias and Robert Wilson used the Holmdel Horn Antenna to detect the cosmic microwave background — proof of the Big Bang, and one of the most consequential radio signals ever received. Station discovery here is powered by Radio-Browser, a free, community-run directory." : {

    },
    "iCloud" : {

    },
    "Keeps your favorites, recently played stations and listening history the same on your devices signed in to iCloud. They are stored in your own iCloud account, where ShoutKit's developer cannot see them. A change here takes effect the next time you open ShoutKit, and turning it off leaves what has already synced in iCloud." : {

    },
    "libogg — BSD" : {
      "comment" : "A license for the Ogg library.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "libvorbis — BSD" : {
      "comment" : "The name of a license for a library.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "License text unavailable — see the project repository." : {

    },
    "Licenses" : {

    },
    "Loop Finished Broadcasts" : {

    },
    "Most stations stream continuously and never end, so this changes nothing for them. A station that broadcasts a fixed-length programme — an hourly newscast, say — stops when it reaches the end; turn this on to have it start over instead." : {

    },
    "Nuke (kean/Nuke), MIT — station logos and Now Playing artwork. Factory (hmlongco/Factory) and AudioStreaming (dimitris-c/AudioStreaming), MIT. AudioStreaming's bundled libogg/libvorbis (sbooth's xcframework builds), BSD. Pulse (kean/Pulse), MIT — a debug-only network inspector, not included in Release builds. The full inventory lives in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md in the repository." : {
      "comment" : "A list of the licenses that ship with the app."
    },
    "Nuke — MIT" : {
      "comment" : "A license for the Nuke package."
